# --- ki-dev-framework ---------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: `.an_framework/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Since v2 the framework
# core is committed into the project as plain files (it is no longer a git
# submodule), so a plain `git clone` reproduces the exact framework version —
# no `--recurse-submodules`, no `git submodule update`. Never add a rule that
# ignores `.an_framework/`. Mind that the broad credential patterns below match
# at ANY depth: the `!.an_framework/**` un-ignore at the very end is what keeps
# them from silently dropping a framework file on `git add`.

.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Operating system — macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*

# Operating system — Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# IDEs / editors — JetBrains
.idea/
.idea_modules/
*.iml

# Credentials — git should not offer these in the first place. `/commit` screens a
# deliberately WIDER set (see step 5 of .an_framework/commands/commit.md) and stops on
# anything this list misses. Keep that asymmetry: the screen may use a broad pattern
# like `*credentials*` because it only stops and asks — here the same pattern would
# silently hide legitimate source such as `src/credentials.ts` from `git status`.
# The three negations must stay directly after `.env.*`. Add your own paths below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.dist
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
*-credentials.json

# Keep the committed framework core intact: re-include anything the broad
# credential globs above would otherwise drop from `.an_framework/`. This line
# must stay LAST — later patterns win in .gitignore.
!.an_framework/**
